<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Ukrainian State</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Kyiv</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Hetman Pavlo Skoropadsky's conservative Ukrainian monarchy of 1918, installed with German backing, which founded Ukraine's Academy of Sciences.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 29 April 1918 German occupation authorities, unhappy with the socialist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-rada">Central Rada</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-peoples-republic">Ukrainian People's Republic</a>, supported a coup by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pavlo-skoropadsky">Pavlo Skoropadsky</a>. A congress of landowners proclaimed him <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">hetman</a>, reviving the title of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cossack-hetmanate">Cossack Hetmanate</a>, and the state was renamed the Ukrainian State.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pavlo-skoropadsky">Skoropadsky</a> ruled with broad powers and a cabinet of largely Russian-educated officials. He restored private property in land, angering peasants, and depended on German troops. Yet the state built a working administration and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-academy-of-sciences-of-ukraine">Ukrainian Academy of Sciences</a>, a national library and new universities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamianets-podilskyi">Kamianets-Podilskyi</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> collapsed in November 1918, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pavlo-skoropadsky">Skoropadsky</a> declared federation with a future non-Bolshevik <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. A revolt led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/directorate-of-ukraine">Directorate</a> gathered strength, and on 14 December 1918 he abdicated and fled to Germany. The Directorate restored the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-peoples-republic">Ukrainian People's Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ukrainian-state.jpg" alt="Ukrainian State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown author Vector: Ιγκόρ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ukraine_(1917%E2%80%931921).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kyiv</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pavlo Skoropadsky, Fedir Lyzohub</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ukrainian, Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Second Hetmanate, Hetmanate of Pavlo Skoropadsky</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=ukrainian-state" aria-label="Ukrainian State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5377 425 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ukrainian State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5697 681L5697 681M5697 681L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5697 681h0M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5697 681h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5697 681h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kyiv. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=ukrainian-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
